# GFlowNet Project Structure

This codebase implements Generative Flow Networks (GFlowNets) in Julia. Key structure:

## Core Architecture

- **[src/GFlowNet.jl](mdc:src/GFlowNet.jl)**: Main module with all exports
- **[src/core/](mdc:src/core/)**: Core mathematical engine (flat structure)
  - **[src/core/types.jl](mdc:src/core/types.jl)**: Core types and abstract interfaces
  - **[src/core/graphs.jl](mdc:src/core/graphs.jl)**: Graph operations (on-demand DAG)
  - **[src/core/policies.jl](mdc:src/core/policies.jl)**: P_F, P_B, Z policy functions
  - **[src/core/flows.jl](mdc:src/core/flows.jl)**: Flow computation with memoization
  - **[src/core/balance.jl](mdc:src/core/balance.jl)**: Balance loss functions
  - **[src/core/sampling.jl](mdc:src/core/sampling.jl)**: Trajectory sampling
  - **[src/core/interface.jl](mdc:src/core/interface.jl)**: High-level model creation
  - **[src/core/multi_start.jl](mdc:src/core/multi_start.jl)**: Multi-start GFlowNets
- **[src/training/](mdc:src/training/)**: Training infrastructure (separate module)
  - **[src/training/configuration.jl](mdc:src/training/configuration.jl)**: TrainingConfig types
  - **[src/training/training.jl](mdc:src/training/training.jl)**: Main training loop
  - **[src/training/objectives.jl](mdc:src/training/objectives.jl)**: Training objectives
  - **[src/training/losses.jl](mdc:src/training/losses.jl)**: Loss computation
  - **[src/training/utils.jl](mdc:src/training/utils.jl)**: Training utilities
  - **[src/training/multi_start_training.jl](mdc:src/training/multi_start_training.jl)**: Multi-start training
- **[src/applications/](mdc:src/applications/)**: Domain implementations (grid world, molecules, etc.)
- **[src/utils/](mdc:src/utils/)**: Utilities (validation, logging, visualization)
- **[examples/](mdc:examples/)**: Usage examples and demos

## High-Level Interface

Users should interact with GFlowNet through high-level functions:
- Use `GFlowNet.create_forward_policy()` instead of manual neural networks
- Use `GFlowNet.TrainingConfig()` and `GFlowNet.train_gflownet()` for training
- Use `GFlowNet.sample_trajectory()` for sampling

## Examples Pattern

Each example follows the same pattern:
1. Define domain-specific state/action types
2. Implement required interface functions (`state_to_features`, `is_applicable`, etc.)
3. Use high-level GFlowNet functions for model creation and training
4. Generate comprehensive results in `results/` directory

## Key Files for Reference

- **[examples/grid_world/grid_world.jl](mdc:examples/grid_world/grid_world.jl)**: Clean example using high-level interface
- **[src/training/training.jl](mdc:src/training/training.jl)**: High-level training functions (train_gflownet, train_step!)
- **[src/training/objectives.jl](mdc:src/training/objectives.jl)**: Training objective enum and configurations
- **[src/core/interface.jl](mdc:src/core/interface.jl)**: Model creation API (create_gflownet, sample_trajectory)
- **[src/applications/grid_world.jl](mdc:src/applications/grid_world.jl)**: Domain-specific convenience function (create_grid_world_gflownet)
